  "notes": "Accounting option (the most detailed of six options: Accounting, Business Analytics, Entrepreneurship, Financial Services, Health Services, Individualized Business, Management and Marketing — all share identical First/Second Year requirements, differing only in Third/Fourth Year option courses). Unlike CMPSC/Premed/Nursing/English, this Intercollege Business B.S. has NO University Park offering — it exists only at Commonwealth Campuses and World Campus. 'etm' marks the courses every later Business course's prereqs assume are done (ACCTG 211, ECON 102/104, ENGL 15). Post-prereq-parser-fix repair, same as BUSINESS-2026.json: ACCTG 211/STAT 200/SCM 200's real prereq is MATH 21 specifically (not MATH 22/26/41/110/140, which this plan's existing 'MATH 21 (or higher)' item also offers) -- and MATH 21 itself real-chains through MATH 4 and MATH 3, neither of which were in this plan, so the auto-scheduler was always falling through to MATH 140 (no prereq) instead of MATH 21, permanently blocking ACCTG 211/STAT 200/SCM 200 downstream. Fixed by removing MATH 21 from the Semester 2 pool (now 'MATH 22 (or higher)') and adding MATH 21 explicitly as its own item (Semester 3) as the single source of truth for that course, same convention as BUSINESS-2026.json/BAIS/CIE. Also added MATH 3 (Semester 1) and MATH 4 (Semester 2) to complete the real chain. Bumped max_credits_per_semester from 17 to 18 to keep 4-year graduation achievable.",
